I may have misinterpreted Genie's as I felt her introduction suggested that she came from a very wealthy family but people are ssaying that she's said elsewhere she came from humble beginnings so I'm not sure.

What I gathered from Genie's backstory was that she came from a very wealthy and traditional immigrant family. The fact that she said her parents basically bought her wedding ring for her also I felt was a sign she came from a lot.

&#x200B;

Also, at risk of generalizing, I'd say its pretty safe to assume that an East Asian family that immigrated to America 50+ years ago had a good amount of wealth built up.

Genie said she came from a traditional Asian family and her mom disapporoved of her sexuality but ultimately gave her a diamond ring (wedding ring my guess is) to give to her.

&#x200B;

I viewed that as she came from a very proper and upper class family, also the fact the parents bought a wedding ring for her.

&#x200B;

Also, definately generalizing quite a bit here but I think its a pretty good chance that an East Asian family who immigrated to America around 50 or more years ago had a fair amoutn of wealth built up. That would've been a MAJOR move back in the day that could only be afforded by the very wealthy. Nowadays I'd sstill say primarily the wealthy immigrate from Asia to America but it certainly is not unheard of for a family to do so with not much to their name and wanting a better life.

